{
  "_readme": [
    "State file for scripts/watch_sources.py.",
    "",
    "It answers a question no other watcher can: the sites we RESEARCH from -",
    "lorcanaplayer.com for pins, lore counters and accessories, the official card",
    "gallery for spoilers - publish lists that nothing on our side reads. The ETL",
    "covers what TCGplayer sells; discovery covers events; this covers the rest,",
    "which until now was a 90-day reminder saying 'go look at this site'.",
    "",
    "TWO SECTIONS",
    "",
    "baselines - what each source listed the last time a person looked. `items`",
    "        is the diffable set (committed in full, so the file itself records",
    "        what was known); `counts` is a per-bucket tally for sources where",
    "        only the aggregate is meaningful. Re-seed with --baseline AFTER",
    "        acting on the findings, never to make a red run go away: baselining",
    "        an unexplained loss bakes it in and the items are never mentioned",
    "        again.",
    "",
    "acks   - one entry per finding key, with a mandatory `why`. An optional",
    "        `until` (YYYY-MM-DD) EXPIRES the ack and re-alerts, which is how",
    "        'revisit when the photo exists' becomes a mechanism instead of a",
    "        promise. Same shape as catalog_watch.json and calendar_watch.json.",
    "",
    "The script NEVER writes to the site's data. Adding a pin mints a permanent",
    "`n` and a permanent photo path; adding a set needs a release date nobody has",
    "published. Those are decisions - this only tells you to look.",
    "",
    "  python scripts/watch_sources.py                       # report",
    "  python scripts/watch_sources.py --explain             # re-measure the match threshold",
    "  python scripts/watch_sources.py --ack KEY --why '...' [--until YYYY-MM-DD]",
    "  python scripts/watch_sources.py --baseline            # accept today as known"
  ],
